# arrivechat.walk (order 1612): an arrival into the open chat, then Back;
# and an arrival, Enter on it, then Back.
#
# Window 23's probe asked whether an arrival in an open chat deafens the
# keys. It opened the list's first row, not "Bench" (`[OPEN]
# peer=f18f4927 messages=0`), so its arrivals landed in another chat and
# its Enter had no message to open; it passed on the broken image without
# asking either question. This one opens "Bench" each time (`bench arrive`
# selects it), so each arrival lands in the chat on the screen and the
# second block's Enter stands on a message: on an image before 1612 the
# second block's Back closes the unseen detail and the last wait fails.
#
#   just m9-walk <rig> scripts/m9-walks/arrivechat.walk <bench elf>
allow key_ms 2000

bench arrive
key enter
wait page=chat
bench arrive
key back
wait page=chats

bench arrive
key enter
wait page=chat
bench arrive
key enter
key back
wait page=chats
dump end
idle 6
